<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69449" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μῡσός</span></b> , ὁ,
			<u>Mysian</u>, <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pers.</u>
			52
		</span></i> (anap.), etc.: proverbially feeble and effeminate, whence prov.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μυσῶν λεία</span>, i. e. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a prey to all</i>, of anything
			that can be plundered with impunity, <i><span class="en">
				Stratt.
				35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1372b33
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Μυσῶν ἔσχατος</span> the
			most worthless of men, <i><span class="en">
				Magn.
				5
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				55
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν λεγομένων</span> M. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἔσχατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					209b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ σοι Μυσόν γε ἥδιον καλεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					521b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				704
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
